    "work_id": "anf-works/aristo-of-pella-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Aristo.1.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Though his work is lost, alike the original and the Latin translation of one “Celsus,” it seems to have been a popular tract among Christians of Cyprian’s time, and the Latin preface is often suffixed to editions of that Father.",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 140,
    "date_range": [
      135,
      175
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/aristo-of-pella-fragments#Aristo.2.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/aristo-of-pella-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Aristo.2.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The work of Aristo is known as the Disputation of Papiscus and Jason, and Celsus tells us that Jason was a Hebrew Christian, while his opponent was a Jew of Alexandria.",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 140,
    "date_range": [
      135,
      175
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/aristo-of-pella-fragments#Aristo.2.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/aristo-of-pella-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Aristo.2.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Now, Papiscus owns himself convinced by the arguments of Jason, and concludes by a request to be baptized.",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 140,
    "date_range": [
      135,
      175
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/aristo-of-pella-fragments#Aristo.2.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/aristo-of-pella-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Aristo.2.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Celsus, who seems to have been a heathen or an Epicurean, derides the work with scornful commiseration; but Origen rebukes this, and affirms his respect for the work.",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 140,
    "date_range": [
      135,
      175
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/aristo-of-pella-fragments#Aristo.2.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/aristo-of-pella-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Aristo.2.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "All this considered, one must think Aristo was “almost persuaded to be a Christian,” and deserves a place among Christian writers.",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 140,
    "date_range": [
      135,
      175
    ],
    "date_confidence": "uncertain",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
